lf_ref":"#/texts/29","text":"10 10"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Frequency (Hz)","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":120.22334798177087,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":109.0,"r":141.0,"t":126.22334798177087},"charspan":[0,14],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/30","text":"Frequency (Hz)"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Frequency {Hz)","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":120.22334798177087,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":210.33333333333334,"r":241.66666666666666,"t":126.22334798177087},"charspan":[0,14],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/31","text":"Frequency {Hz)"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Figure 6 is clearer for mode detection than Figure 7 and shows two modes occurring at 30.2 Hz and 63.5 Hz. This is consistent with the observed response showed in Fig 4 and 5.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":720.8900146484375,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":307.0,"r":540.3333333333334,"t":770.8900146484375},"charspan":[0,175],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/32","text":"Figure 6 is clearer for mode detection than Figure 7 and shows two modes occurring at 30.2 Hz and 63.5 Hz. This is consistent with the observed response showed in Fig 4 and 5."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The calculated modal parameters are given in Table2.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":708.8900146484375,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":322.3333333333333,"r":538.0,"t":721.8900146484375},"charspan":[0,52],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/33","text":"The calculated modal parameters are given in Table2."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"3.3.3 Experimental modal analysis","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":680.2233479817709,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":308.3333333333333,"r":463.6666666666667,"t":692.8900146484375},"charspan":[0,33],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/34","text":"3.3.3 Experimental modal analysis"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"As said before, the calculation is only possible if we possess all the mechanical   parameters but   for   larger shaker   it is often   impossible to block   all the DOFs alternatively and to make it vibrate in order to extract the parameters _ However, as presented in   the  theoretical review, the global mechanical parameters are equivalent to the modal ones","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":589.8900146484375,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":306.6666666666667,"r":540.6666666666666,"t":674.2233479817709},"charspan":[0,363],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/35","text":"As said before, the calculation is only possible if we possess all the mechanical   parameters but   for   larger shaker   it is often   impossible to block   all the DOFs alternatively and to make it vibrate in order to extract the parameters _ However, as presented in   the  theoretical review, the global mechanical parameters are equivalent to the modal ones"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"In [9], Guillaume presented a method for the spectral identification of   modal   parameters by Least Squares Complex Frequency-Domain estimation. The LMS PolyMax method is based on this method and is recognized to be   very fast and accurate for modal estimation [10]","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":515.5566813151042,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":306.0,"r":540.3333333333334,"t":588.8900146484375},"charspan":[0,268],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/36","text":"In [9], Guillaume presented a method for the spectral identification of   modal   parameters by Least Squares Complex Frequency-Domain estimation. The LMS PolyMax method is based on this method and is recognized to be   very fast and accurate for modal estimation [10]"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The corresponding values are given in Table 2.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":430.2233479817708,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":318.3333333333333,"r":507.0,"t":444.8900146484375},"charspan":[0,46],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/37","text":"The corresponding values are given in Table 2."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"We introduced a force with an impact hammer in the two DOFs of the shaker (respectively the table and the body) and measured the acceleration of those DOFs. The LMS PolyMax method computed the transfer functions and estimated the modal parameters with the stabilization diagram presented in Figure 8.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":440.8900146484375,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":307.3333333333333,"r":540.3333333333334,"t":515.8900146484375},"charspan":[0,300],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/38","text":"We introduced a force with an impact hammer in the two DOFs of the shaker (respectively the table and the body) and measured the acceleration of those DOFs. The LMS PolyMax method computed the transfer functions and estimated the modal parameters with the stabilization diagram presented in Figure 8."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Fig. 8. Stabilization   diagram   of the impact on the shaker_ testing","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/2"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":244.55668131510413,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":308.0,"r":539.3333333333334,"t":266.8413718612775},"charspan":[0,70],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/39","text":"Fig. 8. Stabilization   diagram   of the impact on the shaker_ testing"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"Stablllzatlon dlagram Impact testlng on the shaker","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/2"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":411.2233479817708,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":371.6666666666667,"r":485.0,"t":418.2233479817708},"charspan":[0,50],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/40","text":"Stablllzatlon dlagram Impact testlng on the shaker"},{"children